message.content:
Sure! Those numbers are already a pair of latitude/longitude coordinates:

| Latitude | Longitude |
|----------|-----------|
| **37.4224764** | **‑122.0842499** |

If you feed them into the Google Geocoding API (or any reverse‑geocoding service) you’ll get the same spot back – the Googleplex in Mountain View, California.

---

### Quick reverse‑geocode example

```http
GET https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499&key=YOUR_API_KEY
```

**Sample response snippet**

```json
{
  "results": [
    {
      "formatted_address": "1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA",
      "geometry": {
        "location": {
          "lat": 37.4224764,
          "lng": -122.0842499
        },
        ...
      },
      ...
    }
  ],
  "status": "OK"
}
```

So, yes – those coordinates point to the Google headquarters. If you need the address, the API will return it as shown above.
